  "description": "A series of opencast limestone quarries located in the Bois des Lens about 25 km west of N\u00eemes (France) were identified and studied in the 20th century. They are thought to have been brought into use in the fourth century BCE, with peak exploitation occurring during the early Roman Empire.",
